# Example: Faults and Safety
# fair<fault> only restricts the loop of a liveness counterexample. Every
# state is still explored, so a fault that repeats a finite number of
# times can still break a safety assertion.
# Demonstrates: fair<fault> does not limit exploration

action Init:
    faults = 0

atomic fair<fault> action Break:
    if faults < 3:
        faults += 1

always assertion FewFaults:
    return faults < 3
